Second, choose your four subjects wisely. English is compulsory for everyone. The other three subjects must match the course you want to study. For example, Medicine needs English, Biology, Chemistry, and Physics. Law needs English, Literature, Government, and CRS. Choosing the wrong combination can cost you your admission, even if you score very high.

Third, start studying now. JAMB is 400 marks in total, with 100 marks per subject. Practice past questions every day, learn time management, and avoid exam malpractice. Your future starts with your preparation today.